    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d855">

                <pb facs="0694" n="578" xml:id="pg578"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12704.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul General Hanna to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.].</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monterey</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 1, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The peace delegates came to this Consulate early this morning and awakened me.
                    They felt sore and discouraged at the treatment shown them by Constitutionalist
                    officials since their arrival in Tampico. They had decided to quit and wanted me
                    to accompany them to Texas. It was only by the strongest appeals to their
                    patriotism and the advantages of peace that this Consulate induced them to
                    continue on to the conference. We did this because we knew how greatly our
                    President and the Department desired bringing the two parties together. We hope
                    our action pleases you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
